<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Forcalquier</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Forcalquier is a hill town in the Alpes-de-Haute-Provence <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. From the 11th century to 1209 it was the capital of a county formed from the inheritance of the counts of Provence, covering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durance">Durance</a> valley and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisteron">Sisteron</a>. Its citadel hill, former cathedral and Franciscan convent survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/forcalquier.jpg" alt="Forcalquier" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Forcalquier · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Forcalquier_France_Luberon.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
